  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Richmond Maids of Honour are made with shop-bought puff pastry cut into rounds and pressed into a bun tin, then filled with a simple mixture of cream cheese, ground almonds, egg, and lemon that puffs slightly in the oven. The filling should only half-fill the cases before baking: it rises and domes as it bakes. If you overfill, the filling spills over the pastry and burns on the tin."
          }
        ]
      },
