      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Line the tin with puff pastry"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Heat the oven to 200°C (conventional). Lightly grease a 12-hole muffin tin. Roll {{puff-pastry}} on a lightly floured surface to about 3 mm thickness. Cut out 12 rounds using an 8 to 9 cm cutter. Press a round gently into each muffin hole, pressing it into the base and up the sides. Refrigerate the lined tin while you make the filling."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Make the filling"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Beat {{cream-cheese}}, {{unsalted-butter}}, and {{caster-sugar}} together until smooth. Add {{ground-almonds}}, {{eggs}}, the zest and juice of {{lemon}}, {{vanilla-extract}}, and {{nutmeg}}. Mix until just combined. The filling should be thick and spoonsable, not runny."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Fill and bake"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Spoon a heaped teaspoon of filling into each pastry case. The filling should come no more than halfway up the pastry sides; it will rise. Bake for 18 to 22 minutes until the filling is puffed and golden and the pastry has risen and turned deep golden at the edges. The filling will sink slightly as the tarts cool; this is normal. Leave in the tin for 15 minutes before easing out with a palette knife. Serve warm or at room temperature."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
